WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.360
Alright guys, so here is example number two for the monthly bias, I'm looking at AUDUSD

00:06.360 --> 00:08.600
on the monthly timeframe of course.

00:08.600 --> 00:12.040
So now how do you manually identify highs and lows?

00:12.040 --> 00:17.120
So a high and a low is a pattern of three candles, okay?

00:17.120 --> 00:20.320
The first candle is like this.

00:20.320 --> 00:27.480
The second candle is the highest and the third candle is lower than the second candle.

00:27.480 --> 00:29.400
So the second candle has to be the highest.

00:29.400 --> 00:33.000
You can see we have a wick here, wick here and wick here.

00:33.000 --> 00:36.760
The second candle has the highest wick, okay?

00:36.760 --> 00:41.960
Once we have that pattern, right, when the candle closes, that is your high, or you can

00:41.960 --> 00:44.280
simply just use the fractals indicator.

00:44.280 --> 00:52.400
But sometimes fractals might miss these small highs and lows, so you must know what is

00:52.400 --> 00:54.240
high and a low.

00:54.240 --> 01:00.240
So over here, what we have is a purge on the external liquidity and where is the drawn

01:00.240 --> 01:01.240
liquidity?

01:01.240 --> 01:03.480
It's going to be this fair valley gap.

01:03.480 --> 01:09.120
So now let's drop down to the daily timeframe once we have taken out the monthly extended

01:09.120 --> 01:10.280
liquidity.

01:10.280 --> 01:16.640
So now what we want to wait for is a market structure shift and right there you can see

01:16.640 --> 01:20.720
we have a shift in the market structure, beautiful.

01:20.720 --> 01:23.920
So then you can see price fills in the fair valley gap.

01:23.920 --> 01:28.800
So that is going to be our entry, right?

01:28.800 --> 01:32.960
If the fair valley gap is big, you can simply just use the 0.5 level of the fib, which is

01:32.960 --> 01:34.000
going to be this.

01:34.000 --> 01:36.360
So let's say your entry is here.

01:36.360 --> 01:39.440
Let me remove the fib.

01:39.440 --> 01:47.520
Your stop goes above the high and you're simply targeting the monthly drawn liquidity,

01:47.520 --> 01:49.560
which is the fair valley gap.

01:49.560 --> 01:51.160
These two lines is a fair valley gap.

01:51.160 --> 01:53.920
Remember I drew two lines.

01:53.920 --> 01:55.360
So you have your entry.

01:55.360 --> 01:58.640
So let's see what would have happened.

01:58.640 --> 01:59.640
And there you go.

01:59.640 --> 02:00.640
Take profit hit.

02:00.640 --> 02:06.000
You can see we have been bearished throughout these many days.

02:06.000 --> 02:14.000
Now if you were on the one hour timeframe, now let me give you some hints.

02:14.000 --> 02:18.880
You could have taken your entry somewhere around here, maybe here.

02:18.880 --> 02:22.200
If it took out some high or low, but we're going to talk about that later.

02:22.200 --> 02:25.000
Just don't want to confuse you guys.

02:25.000 --> 02:29.960
You can use this as a bread and butter model, just two time frames, right?

02:29.960 --> 02:38.920
Remember time frame alignment, we are for monthly bias, we use monthly, daily and hourly.

02:38.920 --> 02:46.600
For weekly, we use the weekly for our time frame and 15 minutes time frame.

02:46.600 --> 02:55.960
For daily, we use daily one hour and five minutes and for four hour time frame, right?

02:55.960 --> 03:01.760
For intraday bias, we use the four hour, 15 minutes and two minutes.

03:01.760 --> 03:06.480
We're not going to use one minute because it is not reliable.

03:06.480 --> 03:12.480
So price gives us a market structure shift for everybody gap, boom, right there.

